            {
                "content": "# SAN JOAQUIN RIVER BASIN.\n\nflow over Vernal and Nevada falls, by means of which Merced River enters Yosemite Valley.\n\nTenaya Creek enters from the north about 1 mile and Illilouette Creek from the south about 2 miles above the station. Yosemite Creek enters from the north about one-half mile and Bridal Veil Creek from the south about 3 miles below the station.\n\nNo diversions are made above the station except for the small hydro-electric plant which supplies the valley with light and power. The diverted water returns to the river above the station.\n\nNo change has been made in the gage datum. The channel is straight and not subject to much change. The current is sluggish. A fair degree of confidence can be placed in the results at this station.\n\nDischarge measurements of Merced River in Yosemite Valley in 1906, 1907, and 1908.",
